# fixedbugs, defect 557, lane b18-ffi, 2026-10-10 (panel 202's R2; the
# critic's `macro`).
#
# The first group's header defines a macro `twice(x)`, and the second
# group's header declares `static inline int twice(int x)`, which the macro
# turns into no declaration clang can parse when the two are read in this
# order. clang's first error lands in the second header with no note in the
# first, and until 2026-10-10 this was told as that header not compiling,
# where it compiles alone. The two are compiled alone now, and the earlier
# header whose presence makes it fail is named.

extern "fixedbugs-557-macro.h"
    function dbl(x: i64) -> i64

extern "fixedbugs-557-function.h"  #~ ffi_header_refused
    function twice(x: i32) -> i32

function main()
    print(dbl(x: 3))
    print(twice(x: 4))
